WEBVTT

00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:07.815
| look at the moon and remember,

00:00:08.549 --> 00:00:10.651
I look at the stars and long for the past.

00:00:11.418 --> 00:00:14.889
Oh, for those days with the ones I loved.

00:00:16.357 --> 00:00:18.726
The sun illuminates naught but the past,

00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:21.495
and the future remains shrouded in darkness.

00:00:22.496 --> 00:00:24.632
| look again and again into the mirror,

00:00:25.132 --> 00:00:27.067
and yet all I see is the present.

00:00:28.736 --> 00:00:33.073
I will never forget the golden stalks of rice,

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:35.209
the smiles of the children...

00:00:36.577 --> 00:00:41.048
At the very least, I can dream,
until the day comes that I return.

00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:43.384
You're always such a poet.

00:00:44.451 --> 00:00:47.187
You keep saying all that stuff,

00:00:47.588 --> 00:00:49.657
but does a place like that really exist?

00:00:50.257 --> 00:00:53.227
You sure it wasn't a dream, Sensei?

00:00:56.564 --> 00:00:59.633
Beautiful Koto, my beloved child.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.437
I'm sure you'll be able to go there.

00:01:08.242 --> 00:01:08.976
What's this?

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:10.377
For you.

00:01:12.446 --> 00:01:14.315
That which shines and so is divine.

00:01:14.882 --> 00:01:16.450
It's perfect for you.

00:01:17.451 --> 00:01:19.887
| don't get it at all, Sensei.

00:01:20.287 --> 00:01:21.855
You're an idiot, Koto.

00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:24.391
Just look at who raised me.

00:01:26.126 --> 00:01:27.595
Harsh, Koto.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:43.644
I Y O U S O U G I G A\

00:01:53.053 --> 00:01:57.558
A Family's Circumstances
and Its Background

00:01:57.558 --> 00:01:59.026
Chapter 1.
The Past (1)

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:02.129
One splendid, glorious spring day,

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:06.000
A very long time ago
Priest Myoue left the bustle of the city

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:09.203
and moved to the Takao mountains.

00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:18.345
There was something bothering him.

00:02:19.046 --> 00:02:19.647
Flashback

00:02:26.186 --> 00:02:28.522
| drew it because you said
you wanted to see it.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.565
- This isn't working.
- I really saw a dragon!

00:02:38.565 --> 00:02:40.734
The temple is haunted, after all!

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:42.870
The priest is a monster!

00:02:43.671 --> 00:02:46.507
Town Girls It's not like anything
actually happened to them.

00:02:47.174 --> 00:02:47.941
Yeah.

00:02:47.941 --> 00:02:50.044
Father with child | hear one of his
parents was human, and one was a fox.

00:02:50.044 --> 00:02:55.149
Monk
The priest is a man of high morals, but...

00:02:55.149 --> 00:02:59.319
Channeler I've heard he speaks with the gods
of Yin and Yang to do terrifying things...

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:02.456
We wouldn't want
anything bad to happen.

00:03:06.026 --> 00:03:10.164
It was just a moving picture.
They're making too big a deal of it.

00:03:10.698 --> 00:03:12.132
Don't you think so?

00:03:25.012 --> 00:03:29.683
It was thought that there was
no one in his life but his dog,

00:03:30.317 --> 00:03:32.886
but there was something
watching him in secret.

00:03:33.754 --> 00:03:35.656
Koto
The rabbit he'd drawn.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.226
This black rabbit, named Koto,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.962
was drawn on a whim to decorate the walls

00:03:42.362 --> 00:03:44.331
as a picture of the god of the capital.

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:52.272
It seemed to sense something
deep in the man's heart,

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.343
in the way he continued to draw
fictional towns and creatures

00:03:56.343 --> 00:03:58.145
even after voluntarily
leaving the capital.

00:03:58.912 --> 00:04:01.048
Also, it thought he was cute.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.753
In turn, there was something
that watched the rabbit.

00:04:07.054 --> 00:04:09.156
Buddhalocanii.

00:04:10.057 --> 00:04:13.026
This Bodhisattva, whose name means
in part "the eye of the Buddha,”

00:04:13.026 --> 00:04:16.330
knew exactly what the
black rabbit was thinking.

00:04:17.231 --> 00:04:19.433
| will let you borrow my body.

00:04:21.101 --> 00:04:24.738
But in that body, there are limits
to what you can do, are there not?

00:04:25.272 --> 00:04:28.575
| don't think anything will
change unless you force it to.

00:04:29.676 --> 00:04:34.481
Do you think Myoue will notice
how you feel in this state?

00:04:35.482 --> 00:04:39.153
It's Myoue we're talking about here!

00:04:39.887 --> 00:04:41.255
| love being alone!

00:04:44.758 --> 00:04:47.861
There is a strange distortion
in Myoue's heart.

00:04:48.595 --> 00:04:52.299
My eyes exist to see the future,

00:04:52.566 --> 00:04:54.201
and cannot see the past.

00:04:55.068 --> 00:05:00.541
The love you are feeling now
is all that can save him.

00:05:16.723 --> 00:05:17.558
Who are you?

00:05:21.128 --> 00:05:22.062
Koto.

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.869
How did you become human?

00:05:30.571 --> 00:05:31.205
Love!

00:05:31.538 --> 00:05:32.339
Love?

00:05:32.339 --> 00:05:33.006
Love!

00:05:33.006 --> 00:05:33.707
Love?

00:05:33.707 --> 00:05:34.408
Love!

00:05:34.608 --> 00:05:35.175
Love?

00:05:35.175 --> 00:05:36.243
- Yes!
- Hey!

00:05:41.481 --> 00:05:45.052
| don't understand what you're saying.

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:46.386
Don't worry.

00:05:46.787 --> 00:05:49.756
I'll stay by your side until you do.

00:05:53.093 --> 00:05:53.760
Ow!

00:05:55.596 --> 00:05:56.597
Love.

00:05:58.198 --> 00:05:59.633
Labrador

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:04.571
What the rabbit said was crazy,
but as they lived together,

00:06:04.571 --> 00:06:08.742
at some point, something like feelings
towards her developed in the man.

00:06:11.111 --> 00:06:12.179
Yakushimaru!

00:06:13.647 --> 00:06:15.716
Yakushimaru Third Son Time
passed, and soon there were more

00:06:15.716 --> 00:06:17.150
who lived with them.

00:06:21.822 --> 00:06:22.422
What?

00:06:22.589 --> 00:06:25.158
Nothing. Was just wondering
if you were having fun.

00:06:25.559 --> 00:06:26.727
I'm not.

00:06:27.394 --> 00:06:28.195
Neither am.

00:06:28.962 --> 00:06:31.031
Hey, no fighting.

00:06:31.598 --> 00:06:32.633
Older Brother

00:06:32.866 --> 00:06:33.734
Kurama!

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:36.536
Kurama
Eldest Son

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.772
Hot, hot, hot!

00:06:39.873 --> 00:06:41.575
Hey, the yams are ready!

00:06:41.575 --> 00:06:42.309
I'm fine.

00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:43.844
Shall we take them to you?

00:06:44.278 --> 00:06:45.345
I'm fine!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.018
Ow, ow, ow...

00:06:51.018 --> 00:06:52.853
Go easy on him, Kurama.

00:06:52.853 --> 00:06:53.887
Older Sister

00:06:54.254 --> 00:06:55.389
Yase!

00:06:56.256 --> 00:07:01.061
Yase
Second Daughter

00:07:03.563 --> 00:07:05.499
Why did you make me a demon?

00:07:05.499 --> 00:07:07.968
Don't eat the priest, Yase.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:09.970
| hate you too!

00:07:10.337 --> 00:07:12.139
The Kousanji Family Father: Priest Myoue Mother:
Koto Child: Yakushimaru Child: Kurama Child: Yase

00:07:22.149 --> 00:07:25.719
It was a strange family,
but they were happy.

00:07:28.789 --> 00:07:30.891
Shrine

00:07:32.693 --> 00:07:33.827
What to do...

00:07:33.994 --> 00:07:34.928
...about that man?

00:07:35.128 --> 00:07:36.396
We finally chased him...

00:07:36.396 --> 00:07:37.497
...to the mountains.

00:07:37.898 --> 00:07:40.300
Yet he has ruined our honor!

00:07:41.068 --> 00:07:43.236
High Priest, your decision!

00:07:44.304 --> 00:07:46.840
Well, if I must.

00:07:55.115 --> 00:07:56.483
What does it say?

00:07:58.452 --> 00:08:00.487
You don't have to
sugarcoat it.

00:08:00.754 --> 00:08:04.558
"Your family is causing a problem
in the capital. Do something."”

00:08:04.858 --> 00:08:06.893
It's your fault, probably.

00:08:07.094 --> 00:08:07.828
It's Kurama.

00:08:08.028 --> 00:08:08.895
No way.

00:08:08.895 --> 00:08:09.997
I'm back!

00:08:13.333 --> 00:08:14.568
What do we do?

00:08:15.402 --> 00:08:18.171
This was bound to happen sooner or later.

00:08:18.705 --> 00:08:20.774
They have their roles to play.

00:08:20.974 --> 00:08:22.075
There's no helping it.

00:08:24.244 --> 00:08:24.945
Dad...

00:08:26.713 --> 00:08:31.184
| was thinking, maybe Yase and |
should just go back to our pictures.

00:08:31.718 --> 00:08:33.920
Yakushimaru was human to begin with,

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.223
and you should be able to
cover for Mom, right?

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.963
You can get rid of us,
and then remake us.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.766
You have the power to
do that, don't you?

00:08:48.835 --> 00:08:49.636
Dad!

00:08:51.805 --> 00:08:52.873
| don't.

00:08:53.206 --> 00:08:55.842
| won't, Kurama.

00:09:01.214 --> 00:09:07.320
Why don't we all go inside the
world of pictures drawn on the panel walls?

00:09:09.856 --> 00:09:11.158
Mom, that's...

00:09:11.458 --> 00:09:12.726
That's not a bad idea.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:14.795
It's a great idea!

00:09:15.729 --> 00:09:17.197
| love you, Koto!

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.211
It'll be fine.

00:09:32.979 --> 00:09:33.513
Probably.

00:09:34.948 --> 00:09:36.616
It'll be fine!

00:09:37.684 --> 00:09:39.853
Is the capital there called "Kyoto," too?

00:09:41.254 --> 00:09:42.789
There has to be more to it, right?

00:09:43.223 --> 00:09:45.125
| think "Kyoto" is a fine name for it.

00:09:45.392 --> 00:09:47.627
At least change the
characters in the name.

00:09:54.468 --> 00:09:58.538
And so the family moved to the
Looking Glass City,

00:09:58.772 --> 00:10:01.374
and vanished unnoticed.

00:10:03.009 --> 00:10:05.011
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:10:05.011 --> 00:10:06.480
Chapter 2:
The Past (2)

00:10:08.482 --> 00:10:11.451
The new city was ruled over
by Koto and the priest,

00:10:11.451 --> 00:10:13.487
and named the Looking Glass City.

00:10:14.054 --> 00:10:16.623
A world where man and
monster lived side by side.

00:10:20.627 --> 00:10:21.728
Boss!

00:10:21.728 --> 00:10:24.464
The boss is dead!

00:10:25.298 --> 00:10:26.666
Wait, he's alive!

00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:30.837
What I shot was your sinful heart.

00:10:31.438 --> 00:10:34.007
Anything made from a
picture would regenerate,

00:10:34.007 --> 00:10:36.610
and anything broken
would quickly reform.

00:10:37.677 --> 00:10:38.478
This way!

00:10:38.712 --> 00:10:39.646
That way!

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:40.747
This way!

00:10:41.181 --> 00:10:44.551
The family continued to live
in their mountain temple,

00:10:45.218 --> 00:10:48.588
but the children played freely
in their new, huge yard.

00:10:49.356 --> 00:10:50.223
Kurama
Temple

00:10:50.223 --> 00:10:50.957
Yase's
Village

00:10:51.291 --> 00:10:52.759
You are my sunshine.

00:10:53.126 --> 00:10:54.761
My moon! My flower! I love you!

00:10:55.228 --> 00:10:56.563
Would you bear my child?

00:10:56.963 --> 00:10:57.831
We're going home.

00:11:00.233 --> 00:11:05.605
Life in that wonderland
was happy and joyous.

00:11:06.907 --> 00:11:10.610
The days were peaceful and uneventful.

00:11:14.147 --> 00:11:15.615
This is a strange place.

00:11:16.183 --> 00:11:18.218
No one dies. No one is born.

00:11:18.785 --> 00:11:21.821
Everything happens as the
priest and Koto decide it.

00:11:22.422 --> 00:11:24.824
Well, it's good that there's no war.

00:11:25.759 --> 00:11:28.195
In other words,
everything else is bad?

00:11:29.229 --> 00:11:30.564
| didn't say that.

00:11:30.997 --> 00:11:32.065
Don't get so angry.

00:11:32.299 --> 00:11:33.266
I'm not!

00:11:34.234 --> 00:11:36.203
Don't you think it's strange?

00:11:36.836 --> 00:11:39.105
How long are we supposed
to stay children?

00:11:41.942 --> 00:11:44.277
It got away again!

00:11:45.912 --> 00:11:48.114
You seem like you're
having fun every day.

00:11:48.548 --> 00:11:49.649
Of course.

00:11:49.849 --> 00:11:52.619
I'm happy as long as I can be with Mom!

00:11:55.322 --> 00:11:57.691
And it's convenient how
everything fixes itself.

00:11:57.691 --> 00:11:59.826
And once in a while,
new things appear.

00:12:00.193 --> 00:12:02.028
There's even that new train station!

00:12:02.529 --> 00:12:04.130
What is it that you don't like?

00:12:06.099 --> 00:12:07.867
It's not that I don't like it...

00:12:08.201 --> 00:12:11.037
It makes you uneasy,
having everything the way you want it.

00:12:44.904 --> 00:12:45.438
Koto.

00:12:46.873 --> 00:12:48.875
You had the same dream
again, didn't you?

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.544
What will you do if you leave?

00:12:51.945 --> 00:12:53.713
Go back to being a rabbit,
after all this?

00:12:53.713 --> 00:12:54.781
Dream
Journal

00:12:54.781 --> 00:12:56.149
You knew, then.

00:12:57.751 --> 00:12:59.486
| made a promise with the Buddha.

00:13:00.053 --> 00:13:03.757
My selfishness has caused
things to drag on this long.

00:13:05.225 --> 00:13:08.628
So what do you gain
by rushing things now?

00:13:11.298 --> 00:13:14.067
| am simply a rabbit,
drawn on paper.

00:13:15.335 --> 00:13:18.772
| was only given human form by
the compassion of the Buddha.

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:24.844
| promised to return this body as
soon as you reciprocated my love.

00:13:26.579 --> 00:13:27.981
| knew this!

00:13:28.548 --> 00:13:32.952
My presence here will bring
some great evil to this world.

00:13:34.154 --> 00:13:38.124
But still, each time I saw your face,
and those of the children,

00:13:38.391 --> 00:13:42.696
| told myself, "One more day!
Just one more day!"

00:13:44.964 --> 00:13:49.002
The eyes of Buddhalocanii
see all of reality.

00:13:49.969 --> 00:13:54.007
It is only a matter of time
before my dreams become reality.

00:13:54.908 --> 00:13:59.612
You knew all that, and yet have
pretended to know nothing.

00:13:59.913 --> 00:14:01.047
Very selfish.

00:14:01.948 --> 00:14:02.949
What about you?

00:14:05.185 --> 00:14:07.654
That's right. I'm the same.

00:14:08.621 --> 00:14:10.357
| knew and yet I could do nothing.

00:14:11.257 --> 00:14:12.459
| was afraid.

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:16.129
Much more afraid of losing you...

00:14:18.565 --> 00:14:19.532
Let us go together.

00:14:20.967 --> 00:14:23.136
| will never leave you alone.

00:14:35.749 --> 00:14:38.385
It was a sudden goodbye.

00:14:41.421 --> 00:14:43.857
With their parents gone from
the Looking Glass City,

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.860
the children were left only
with memories of their parents

00:14:47.227 --> 00:14:53.233
and a promise that they knew
not when would be fulfilled.

00:14:55.034 --> 00:14:57.036
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:14:57.036 --> 00:14:58.571
Chapter 3: Present
(1)/ The Looking Glass

00:14:58.571 --> 00:15:00.206
<i>The Kousanji Family Jekkkkkkkkkkkikkkk *kkkkkkik
*kkkkkkkkkkkkkkk Mvoue Child: Kurama Child: Yase</i>

00:15:07.947 --> 00:15:11.451
| don't know how they live every day
like this without getting bored.

00:15:13.286 --> 00:15:15.989
It's not like there's anything to report.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:20.927
Right?

00:15:27.367 --> 00:15:29.602
Shut up already!

00:15:35.141 --> 00:15:37.043
Good boy, good boy.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.845
Okay, watch carefully.

00:15:38.845 --> 00:15:40.380
You want this, right? Right?

00:15:40.847 --> 00:15:42.549
If you want it...

00:15:42.816 --> 00:15:44.684
Fetch!

00:15:52.692 --> 00:15:53.426
Okay.

00:16:00.333 --> 00:16:03.269
I'm surprised you remember
something from that long ago.

00:16:03.269 --> 00:16:07.173
Every memory I have
with you is unforgettable.

00:16:08.274 --> 00:16:09.976
| get that a lot.

00:16:10.276 --> 00:16:12.145
They say my body keeps getting updated,

00:16:12.145 --> 00:16:14.647
but my head stays the same.

00:16:16.316 --> 00:16:17.217
Yeah.

00:16:18.117 --> 00:16:20.553
You've gotten a lot bigger, Yakushimaru.

00:16:21.921 --> 00:16:23.957
I've been left behind.

00:16:26.659 --> 00:16:27.827
I'm sorry, Myoue.

00:16:27.827 --> 00:16:29.028
It was just out of habit...

00:16:29.562 --> 00:16:31.097
| don't mind.

00:16:31.097 --> 00:16:34.901
No. Everything changes for a reason.

00:16:36.135 --> 00:16:38.605
I'm sure there's a reason
for your name, as well.

00:16:40.106 --> 00:16:44.511
Even so, I'm happy you
still come to see me.

00:16:50.416 --> 00:16:51.451
Of course I do.

00:16:58.057 --> 00:16:59.225
| get it.

00:16:59.225 --> 00:17:00.960
February 8th (Sat)
Don't get so mad.

00:17:01.094 --> 00:17:01.561
Huh?

00:17:01.928 --> 00:17:03.096
I'm not slacking!

00:17:03.429 --> 00:17:05.365
You guys just take this too seriously.

00:17:06.866 --> 00:17:08.134
I'm listening.

00:17:08.735 --> 00:17:09.636
| said I'm sorry.

00:17:16.342 --> 00:17:16.809
Yeah.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:18.244
Right.

00:17:18.978 --> 00:17:19.479
Right.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:21.981
See you tomorrow. Yeah.

00:17:25.652 --> 00:17:27.387
You ditched the Council again?

00:17:29.489 --> 00:17:33.359
No one quite knows what to
do with our Priest Myoue.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:35.628
I'm fine as I am.

00:17:36.529 --> 00:17:37.564
I'm just a stand-in.

00:17:42.435 --> 00:17:44.571
But your prayer beads are
important to you, right?

00:17:47.807 --> 00:17:50.109
If you hate it that much, then quit.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:51.744
| can't.

00:17:52.478 --> 00:17:53.479
You tried?

00:17:54.013 --> 00:17:54.814
Of course.

00:17:55.148 --> 00:17:56.416
It was horrible.

00:17:58.418 --> 00:17:59.652
I'll tell you some day.

00:17:59.953 --> 00:18:01.054
You'll laugh.

00:18:02.055 --> 00:18:04.791
Anyway, I'm just holding
on to these beads,

00:18:05.925 --> 00:18:09.395
and until they come back,
this'll still be the Looking Glass.

00:18:09.996 --> 00:18:11.297
Sounds rough.

00:18:11.631 --> 00:18:12.932
You sound disinterested.

00:18:13.232 --> 00:18:15.735
You and I are in such
different positions.

00:18:16.202 --> 00:18:18.871
And more than anything,
| like this place.

00:18:19.238 --> 00:18:20.106
| see.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.310
Oh, my poor little noble Myoue!

00:18:27.614 --> 00:18:28.781
It hurts you, doesn't it?

00:18:30.016 --> 00:18:31.784
Are you going to make
me feel better?

00:18:32.118 --> 00:18:33.486
Am I good enough for you?

00:18:34.087 --> 00:18:35.455
You're the only one for me.

00:18:35.788 --> 00:18:37.991
Do you say that to all the girls?

00:18:38.524 --> 00:18:39.559
No, no.

00:18:44.931 --> 00:18:46.265
You want to stay the night?

00:18:46.866 --> 00:18:51.871
No... just gonna take a nap.

00:19:01.114 --> 00:19:06.686
| hope someday, someone comes

00:19:07.387 --> 00:19:10.023
who can take you away from here.

00:19:15.728 --> 00:19:16.996
Someday I'll return,

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.366
bringing with me the
beginning and the end.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:21.968
| promise.

00:19:22.702 --> 00:19:24.737
Just wait for me, Myoue.

00:19:30.309 --> 00:19:31.210
Myoue!

00:19:31.411 --> 00:19:33.179
Something weird's happening outside.

00:19:47.226 --> 00:19:49.662
Get me that analysis now!
What's going on?

00:19:50.363 --> 00:19:53.599
We almost never get a chance like this! You there!
They're acting like the gates of hell have opened.

00:19:53.599 --> 00:19:55.501
Stop standing around!
You might not be

00:19:55.501 --> 00:19:58.137
It's do or die time!
too far off. There's also

00:19:58.137 --> 00:20:01.441
the possibility that
the gates in question are pearly.

00:20:09.048 --> 00:20:10.216
So beautiful...

00:20:11.117 --> 00:20:12.785
| want one for this place, too.

00:20:13.119 --> 00:20:14.821
Can't someone go get it for me?

00:20:19.158 --> 00:20:20.326
Kurama, please!

00:20:20.827 --> 00:20:21.994
Give me a lift!

00:20:23.062 --> 00:20:24.464
| don't have it! It broke!

00:20:24.831 --> 00:20:26.132
That's why I'm asking you!

00:20:28.234 --> 00:20:30.369
It's not repairing itself. Strange.

00:20:30.369 --> 00:20:32.004
No clue! I don't know, either!

00:20:33.906 --> 00:20:36.609
That's right! It's just a hunch,
but I can't shake it!

00:20:37.176 --> 00:20:38.411
Just help me out, okay?

00:20:40.113 --> 00:20:41.948
| know that light.

00:20:42.715 --> 00:20:45.051
| saw it once, with him.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.354
Have you returned...

00:20:49.088 --> 00:20:49.922
Priest?!

00:21:32.365 --> 00:21:33.933
No good, Sis.

00:21:33.933 --> 00:21:35.735
It's not here.

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:40.173
Damn! I thought
| finally had it!

00:21:40.773 --> 00:21:43.776
I'll follow it to the ends
of the stars if I have to!

00:21:52.385 --> 00:21:53.953
Are you from around here?

00:21:55.288 --> 00:21:57.690
I'm with the Shrine...

00:21:58.057 --> 00:21:59.358
Have you seen a rabbit?

00:21:59.659 --> 00:22:00.526
A black one.

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.361
With red eyes.

00:22:02.361 --> 00:22:03.696
And it's got ears.

00:22:03.863 --> 00:22:05.598
And a mouth.

00:22:05.832 --> 00:22:07.567
And it had legs, too!

00:22:10.236 --> 00:22:11.237
Shrine?

00:22:12.872 --> 00:22:13.739
You don't know it?

00:22:15.708 --> 00:22:18.110
What backwater plane is he from?

00:22:21.681 --> 00:22:22.248
Hey.

00:22:25.751 --> 00:22:28.120
Listen, what's this place called?

00:22:29.922 --> 00:22:30.957
Where are we?

00:22:31.524 --> 00:22:33.926
What number plane are we on?

00:22:35.695 --> 00:22:37.763
Nothing, huh?

00:22:43.903 --> 00:22:44.737
Kyoto.

00:22:46.038 --> 00:22:47.840
Kyoto, the Looking Glass City.

00:22:48.841 --> 00:22:51.844
| don't know what this "plane”
thing is you're talking about.

00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:01.320
This place has been off limits
to civilians for centuries.

00:23:02.622 --> 00:23:06.492
This isn't a place normal kids
can get into by themselves.

00:23:08.594 --> 00:23:10.563
Who the hell are you?

00:23:12.932 --> 00:23:16.135
Once, when many planets
intermingled and

00:23:16.702 --> 00:23:19.639
the boundary between man
and god was vague...

00:23:20.673 --> 00:23:26.045
There was a tale of a particular family.
A tale of love and rebirth.

00:23:26.345 --> 00:23:26.846
Koto!

00:23:28.347 --> 00:23:29.982
From the center of plane 1.

00:23:30.449 --> 00:23:32.251
A member of the Inari squad, answering

00:23:32.251 --> 00:23:35.254
directly to the High Priest
of the Unified Organization, the Shrine.

00:23:36.055 --> 00:23:38.591
I've come to find my mom.

00:23:47.233 --> 00:23:53.673
I'd even cut things off, (Ouch!)
to prove the fact I exist.

00:23:55.508 --> 00:24:01.614
Though eternal lies surround me,
they're my safety line.

00:24:03.416 --> 00:24:09.855
"Wanna take you high?"
The galaxy shakes. You smile.

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:18.030
I want to touch you. I don't want
to hear that it's forbidden.

00:24:19.899 --> 00:24:23.536
Moved to emotion by arguments,
| cast aside reason.

00:24:23.536 --> 00:24:28.641
I enter a game of risk that's
devoid of reason.

00:24:31.911 --> 00:24:36.649
It's resplendent with rare pain.

00:24:40.086 --> 00:24:45.157
Mistaking the real for the unreal.

00:24:48.294 --> 00:24:52.264
It transcends all understanding.

00:24:52.264 --> 00:24:53.165
So, fight!

00:24:56.435 --> 00:24:57.169
So, fight!

00:25:00.539 --> 00:25:01.273
So, fight!

00:25:08.581 --> 00:25:09.482
So, fight!

00:25:10.049 --> 00:25:12.018
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:25:12.385 --> 00:25:15.021
Do you ever find yourself
remembering the past

00:25:15.021 --> 00:25:17.089
when you come to a new place?

00:25:17.757 --> 00:25:21.127
You always remember the bad things.

00:25:21.427 --> 00:25:23.996
But sometimes you remember
some of the good things, too!

00:25:26.098 --> 00:25:29.268
| wonder what everybody from
the Shrine is doing right now.

00:25:29.435 --> 00:25:30.736
Are they sad without me?

00:25:31.037 --> 00:25:34.140
Or are they glad to be rid of me?

00:25:34.140 --> 00:25:37.276
Wikat Canoe wes & Lifiie Ssier
Next time: "What Came was a Little Sister!"

00:25:37.576 --> 00:25:39.378
A little sister is here!
